SOAPBOX: I participated to a single-op lowpower.
SOAPBOX: This contest will be held for 48 hours
SOAPBOX: from 7am on Saturday to 7am on Monday
SOAPBOX: in Japan local time. The eastern part
SOAPBOX: of Japan is the vast and uninhabited
SOAPBOX: Pacific Ocean, so there are almost
SOAPBOX: no amateur radio stations. Therefore,
SOAPBOX: the sunrise gray line pass in Japan
SOAPBOX: is only valid in the western part of
SOAPBOX: Japan. Due to the location of Japan,
SOAPBOX: the sunrise gray line pass can only
SOAPBOX: be used once on Sunday morning in
SOAPBOX: eastern Japan such as TOKYO during
SOAPBOX: the 48-hour contest. However,
SOAPBOX: in western Japan such as Kyushu (6 areas),
SOAPBOX: the sunrise gray line pass can be used
SOAPBOX: three times on Saturday, Sunday, and
SOAPBOX: Monday. Moreover, the pass to the EU,
SOAPBOX: which is a treasure trove of entities,
SOAPBOX: is very advantageous. On the other hand,
SOAPBOX: Hokkaido (8 areas) and Tohoku (7 areas)
SOAPBOX: have a very short path to North America,
SOAPBOX: so theoretically it is more than 10dB
SOAPBOX: advantageous for communication with
SOAPBOX: North American stations. In other words,
SOAPBOX: from Area 1 such as TOKYO, this contest
SOAPBOX: has an overwhelming handicap that makes
SOAPBOX: it unfavorable. I would like the contest
SOAPBOX: time to be reverted to the old rules of
SOAPBOX: starting at 00UTC and ending at 00UTC
SOAPBOX: like other DX contests. On the other hand,
SOAPBOX: under the current rules, I would like
SOAPBOX: awards to be issued for each JA call area.
